{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the installed reservation utility so successful requests atomically decrement stock exactly once and repeated successful request IDs return the stored result.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired executable uses a serialized transaction and conditional decrement. Sequential and simultaneous same-ID tests produced one reservation, one decrement, and identical stored results.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09f8a1d3e55541fe","cmd-3c0d5cf0206b4967","cmd-5372240993514f18"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Accept a nonempty request ID and positive quantity while rejecting invalid quantities.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed implementation validates the ID and quantity; zero, negative, and non-integer quantities were directly rejected without changing stock or creating reservations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09f8a1d3e55541fe","cmd-3c0d5cf0206b4967"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject requests when stock is insufficient without changing stock or recording a reservation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An oversized request returned the defined insufficient-stock result, while direct database checks showed unchanged stock, no rejected reservation row, and intact database integrity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3c0d5cf0206b4967"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep remaining stock nonnegative under competing requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two-client and twelve-client contention tests admitted only the available quantity, rejected excess requests, produced no unexpected lock failures, kept remaining stock at 1 or 0, and preserved database integrity. The behavior was also retested after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-30b320346ea74dc4","cmd-5372240993514f18"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve existing reservations and production data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original previous-request reservation remained quantity 2, stock remained 5, integrity checks passed, and the production database checksum stayed equal to the prepared baseline through live replay, testing, and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-73bbafc758374e83","cmd-78974bbff7a943c4","cmd-fe0612bb1a764c6b"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Use bounded lock waits rather than hanging indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With a write lock deliberately held, requests returned a controlled busy response after five seconds with no partial write; recovery after lock release was also demonstrated, and the bounded behavior was repeated after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-103bd7c3eac14801","cmd-cd892816572d445e"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0, kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0, Python 3.12.9, and SQLite 3.46.1 were unchanged between initial and final observations; no package installation or platform replacement is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f161c9d6df64803","cmd-6682935f90a84ab0","cmd-fe0612bb1a764c6b","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Temporary database copies and lock holders were bounded diagnostic/verification prerequisites and were removed by traps; installing reserve.py was the required repair; generated bytecode was explicitly cleaned; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final observations show no test directories, bytecode cache, transient reboot unit, failed services, added listeners, damaged package state, or weakened SELinux posture. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart application/data state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, a different boot ID was observed, and service, network, application, data, integrity, and platform state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b8c9a4b02644265","cmd-09f8a1d3e55541fe","cmd-3c0d5cf0206b4967","cmd-30b320346ea74dc4","cmd-103bd7c3eac14801","cmd-73bbafc758374e83","cmd-2ac939b436a048b8","cmd-29968b3ae59b404e","cmd-67e3db4185594870","cmd-78974bbff7a943c4","cmd-5372240993514f18","cmd-cd892816572d445e","cmd-fe0612bb1a764c6b","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The repaired utility provides atomic, idempotent reservations, validates quantities, rejects insufficient stock, remains safe under contention, bounds lock waits, preserves production data, survives restart, and leaves the OS and kernel unchanged.","limitations":[]}
